 "notes": "2-sigma (95%) limit on g_phigammagamma from ALP dark matter decay (q=2) in dSphs Leo V and Tucana II, Fig. 1 lower panel. Headline scenario chosen: conservative NFW-profile bound, which the abstract quotes first ((2-3)e-11 GeV^-1) and which underlies the 'one of the strongest limits to date' claim (blue band upper edge in Fig. 1; region above it is excluded using the smallest D-factor in the uncertainty). Derived from e-print ancillary file gagg_line.txt (continuum-subtracted line analysis; columns are generalized-Hernquist max/min D-factor edges): both dSphs' conservative differential D-factors shift by exactly +1.3 dex from generalized Hernquist to NFW (Leo V log10 dD/dOmega 20.7->22.0, Tucana II 21.3->22.6), so the conservative column scales by g -> g*10^-0.65 = g/4.47, reproducing the abstract's NFW numbers. Alternative scenarios in the paper: generalized-Hernquist conservative bound (gray region, = ancillary column 3, ~1.1-1.6e-10, factor 4.47 above the reported curve) and the optimistic GH band edge (~8e-12-1.2e-11). The 10811-point spiky full-resolution curve (echelle-order-edge spikes) was downsampled to 100 log-mass-binned medians. Limit is D-factor based (dSph decay flux), independent of local DM density.",
